Z||000000||Simple Fiero||07-29-2001||06:38 PM||||K let me start by saying that I am not that mechanically inclined. There was a bit of a stumbling of my car at a steady press of the gas pedal. So I thought great I will take it to crappy tire and get a scope on it and lock down the problem and get them to help me, then do the work myself. So I book the appointment and the lady said it would be no problem, so I get there and the guy at the counter goes "Oh we can't work that" I was like "WHAT". He goes we dont' work on fieros, so I ask why. He tells me that there is a engine problem on them so that he can't hook them up to the scope. One has anyone else heard of this problem?  So if this isn't true why was midas more than willing to the scope for me. So Canadian Tire can ****'in bite me. ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Jay||07-29-2001||06:43 PM||||Canadian Tire are a bunch of teenage pimple faced morons!  What is the difference between a Fiero with a 2.8 and a Cavalier with a 2.8?  Nothing!  At least not significant enough to get your shorts all in a knot.  Canadian tire is notorious for screwing up Fieros and then after they've dismantled the engine, craddle and suspension they hand it back to you in a pile and say we can't fix it!  Don't laugh, it's happened to someone here in Toronto, he's now sueing!  I'll never go there for any work...ever...for any car!!  They screwed up on my 84 Fiero about 10 years ago, never again.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
