Z||000006||p4n1c||07-29-2001||08:09 PM||||Actually the 2.8 in the Fiero is the exact same engine that is in my Cutlass, a Beretta, Cavalier, etc.  The only difference is that I have DIS and power steering.  There is just more restriction in the intake and exhaust which leads them to have lower HP numbers.<P>If you check the cam lift, valve size and compression ratio(8.9:1), they are the exact same.  The reason they aren't interchangable is because there are different mount points for the accessories and engine.<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 07-29-2001).]||||reg||1
